A||||1||rodmcneill||Body panel retainers?||||5||
Z||000000||rodmcneill||08-26-2001||11:52 PM||||Does anyone know how many types of plastic-nylon retainers the Fiero body-interior uses. I see packages for sale on E-bay all the time, all different shapes and sizes. I don't have a P22 manual(yet) so I don't know where they all go since I havn't done any body work yet. Any sites that show where they all go?||||reg||5
Z||000001||mbramble||08-27-2001||12:07 AM||||Try <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierostore.com</A>  and check under Moldings and then fastener kits.  They show you where many of the fasteners go.  You can also buy fasteners at <A HREF="http://www.ardeldistributors.com/category.html?UCIDs=414669%7C656537" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ardeldistributors.com/category.html?UCIDs=414669%7C656537</A>  . These are the guys who have most of the fasteners for auction on ebay.  You can often get some very good prices when you buy the quantities they auction.  More fasteners than you will need in some cases but if you have more than one car, or go in with someone else it might be worth it.  I have made several orders from them and they are a good company to deal with....<BR><p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 08-27-2001).]||||reg||1
